{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:38:44.182Z","ordinal":5106,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f08cea1c87d2bcd83537dcb282ce","summary_text":["**Evaluating report usability**\n\nThe exported report is currently detailed but quite useful. I can calculate and include `reviewFlags`, like noting any input receipt issues and comparing the `strongestMeasuredJoint` to the structured predicted strongest. If there’s a mismatch, it might be significant to flag that: \"Predicted strongest J4 differs from largest measured torque range Joint 2; review before handoff.\" This would highlight any discrepancies for reviewers, emphasizing the superior value of the app over generic AI. Adding a \"Review note\" callout could enhance clarity.","**Enhancing UI for reviews**\n\nI’m thinking it might be valuable to add a \"Review before handoff\" section in the UI, especially if there’s a mismatch in measured torque. This could be a low-effort, high-value enhancement. I could pull the strongest measured value directly from `analyzeWindow` or telemetry data instead of just the message text. By using a helper in `investigationReport`, I can define a function that returns a flag if it detects discrepancies. Including this in the report and showing a `reviewFlag` in the UI would help maintain transparency."],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1789259917012,"completed_at_ms":1789259924182}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:38:44.184Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f08cea1c87d2bcd83537dcb282ce","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating report usability**\n\nThe exported report is currently detailed but quite useful. I can calculate and include `reviewFlags`, like noting any input receipt issues and comparing the `strongestMeasuredJoint` to the structured predicted strongest. If there’s a mismatch, it might be significant to flag that: \"Predicted strongest J4 differs from largest measured torque range Joint 2; review before handoff.\" This would highlight any discrepancies for reviewers, emphasizing the superior value of the app over generic AI. Adding a \"Review note\" callout could enhance clarity.","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Enhancing UI for reviews**\n\nI’m thinking it might be valuable to add a \"Review before handoff\" section in the UI, especially if there’s a mismatch in measured torque. This could be a low-effort, high-value enhancement. I could pull the strongest measured value directly from `analyzeWindow` or telemetry data instead of just the message text. By using a helper in `investigationReport`, I can define a function that returns a flag if it detects discrepancies. Including this in the report and showing a `reviewFlag` in the UI would help maintain transparency.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:38:45.165Z","ordinal":5108,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f09412d087d2918ca43970c98840","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The rendered flow works end to end, including jumping the robot to 6.063 s and exporting Markdown. One useful gap remains visible: the model names J4, while the largest measured torque range is J2. I’m turning that disagreement into an explicit review note so the product demonstrates human verification instead of quietly presenting one answer as truth."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789259924185,"completed_at_ms":1789259925165}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:38:45.166Z","ordinal":5109,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f09412d087d2918ca43970c98840","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The rendered flow works end to end, including jumping the robot to 6.063 s and exporting Markdown. One useful gap remains visible: the model names J4, while the largest measured torque range is J2. I’m turning that disagreement into an explicit review note so the product demonstrates human verification instead of quietly presenting one answer as truth."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:39:01.805Z","ordinal":5110,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f0951f9887d2b994da09a1b0c185","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ReCPXbKDexxOgFRYFVihXDjj","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/predictionReview.ts\\n+import { selectWindow } from '../lib/data';\\n+import type { DemoData, Interval } from '../types';\\n+import { structuredPrediction } from './predictionBrief';\\n+\\n+export type PredictionReview = {\\n+  predictedJoint: string;\\n+  largestRangeJoint: string;\\n+  note: string;\\n+};\\n+\\n+/** Surface a model/measurement disagreement without treating either quantity as physical truth. */\\n+export function reviewPrediction(data: DemoData, interval: Interval, output?: string): PredictionReview | undefined {\\n+  const prediction = structuredPrediction(output);\\n+  if (!prediction?.strongest_joint) return;\\n+  const window = selectWindow(data, interval);\\n+  const strongest = window.channels\\n+    .map(channel => ({ channel, range: Math.max(...channel.values) - Math.min(...channel.values) }))\\n+    .sort((a, b) => b.range - a.range)[0];\\n+  if (!strongest) return;\\n+  const largestRangeJoint = `J${strongest.channel.id.replace('joint_', '')}`;\\n+  if (largestRangeJoint === prediction.strongest_joint) return;\\n+  return {\\n+    predictedJoint: prediction.strongest_joint,\\n+    largestRangeJoint,\\n+    note: `OpenTSLM highlights ${prediction.strongest_joint}, while ${largestRangeJoint} has the largest measured torque range. Review both signals before sharing this handoff.`,\\n+  };\\n+}\\n*** Add File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/predictionReview.test.ts\\n+import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\n+import type { DemoData } from '../types';\\n+import { reviewPrediction } from './predictionReview';\\n+\\n+const channels = Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, index) => ({\\n+  id: `joint_${index + 1}`, name: `Joint ${index + 1}`, unit: 'Nm', values: index === 1 ? [-3, 2] : [0, index === 3 ? 2 : 1],\\n+}));\\n+const data: DemoData = {\\n+  recording: { id: 'r', name: 'R', durationSeconds: 2, sampleRateHz: 1000, displaySampleRateHz: 1000, sourceUrl: '', archive: '', channelCount: 7, eventCount: 0 },\\n+  times: [0, .001], channels, detail: { startSeconds: 0, endSeconds: 1, times: [0, .001], channels }, events: [],\\n+};\\n+const prediction = (joint: string) => `Answer: {\\\"contact\\\":true,\\\"event_type\\\":\\\"accidental\\\",\\\"onset_ms\\\":1,\\\"strongest_joint\\\":\\\"${joint}\\\",\\\"affected_joints\\\":[\\\"${joint}\\\"],\\\"evidence_start_ms\\\":1,\\\"evidence_end_ms\\\":2}`;\\n+\\n+describe('prediction review', () => {\\n+  it('flags a visible model and measurement disagreement', () => {\\n+    expect(reviewPrediction(data, { start: 0, end: .002 }, prediction('J4'))).toEqual({\\n+      predictedJoint: 'J4', largestRangeJoint: 'J2',\\n+      note: 'OpenTSLM highlights J4, while J2 has the largest measured torque range. Review both signals before sharing this handoff.',\\n+    });\\n+  });\\n+\\n+  it('does not manufacture a review issue when the strongest joints agree', () => {\\n+    expect(reviewPrediction(data, { start: 0, end: .002 }, prediction('J2'))).toBeUndefined();\\n+  });\\n+});\\n*** Update File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx\\n@@\\n import { predictionBrief, predictionCue, structuredPrediction, type PredictionCue } from './predictionBrief';\\n+import { reviewPrediction } from './predictionReview';\\n@@\\n         const brief = predictionBrief(m.modelOutput);\\n         const cue = m.status === 'complete' ? predictionCue(m.modelOutput, m.interval) : undefined;\\n+        const review = m.status === 'complete' ? reviewPrediction(m.telemetry, m.interval, m.modelOutput) : undefined;\\n@@\\n-              {brief ? <><section className=\\\"prediction-summary\\\"><h3>{brief.title}</h3><div className=\\\"prediction-facts\\\">{brief.strongest && <span>Predicted strongest joint <strong>{brief.strongest}</strong></span>}{brief.onset !== undefined && <span>Predicted onset <strong>{brief.onset} ms</strong> into the window</span>}</div><p className=\\\"prediction-caution\\\">OpenTSLM prediction · not a verified physical diagnosis.</p></section>{measuredText && <section className=\\\"measured-summary\\\"><h3>Measured torque</h3><p>{measuredText}</p></section>}</> : m.text ? <AnswerText text={m.text}/> : null}\\n+              {brief ? <><section className=\\\"prediction-summary\\\"><h3>{brief.title}</h3><div className=\\\"prediction-facts\\\">{brief.strongest && <span>Predicted strongest joint <strong>{brief.strongest}</strong></span>}{brief.onset !== undefined && <span>Predicted onset <strong>{brief.onset} ms</strong> into the window</span>}</div><p className=\\\"prediction-caution\\\">OpenTSLM prediction · not a verified physical diagnosis.</p></section>{measuredText && <section className=\\\"measured-summary\\\"><h3>Measured torque</h3><p>{measuredText}</p></section>}{review && <section className=\\\"review-note\\\"><h3>Review note</h3><p>{review.note}</p></section>}</> : m.text ? <AnswerText text={m.text}/> : null}\\n*** Update File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/investigationReport.ts\\n@@\\n import { structuredPrediction } from './predictionBrief';\\n+import { reviewPrediction } from './predictionReview';\\n@@\\n   const receiptIssue = answer.mode === 'assistant'\\n     ? inputReceiptIssue(answer.inputTrace, data.recording.id, answer.interval)\\n     : undefined;\\n+  const predictionReview = answer.mode === 'assistant' ? reviewPrediction(data, answer.interval, answer.modelOutput) : undefined;\\n@@\\n       inputReceipt: answer.inputTrace ?? null, evidence: answer.evidence },\\n+    reviewNotes: predictionReview ? [predictionReview.note] : [],\\n@@\\n   const ans