g>Show predicted moment in 3D</strong><ArrowUpRight size={12}/></button></li>}\n+              {cue && <li><button onClick={() => onRobotPrediction(cue)}><span>1</span><strong>Show generated onset cue in 3D</strong><ArrowUpRight size={12}/></button></li>}\n               {m.evidence.map((e, i) => <li key={i}><button onClick={() => onEvidence(e)}><span>{cue ? 2 : 1}</span><strong>Inspect exact seven-channel input</strong><SlidersHorizontal size={12}/></button></li>)}\n-              <li><button onClick={() => onCompare(m.interval)}><span>{cue ? 3 : m.evidence.length ? 2 : 1}</span><strong>Compare with a reference window</strong><ArrowUpRight size={12}/></button></li>\n+              <li><button onClick={() => onCompare(m.interval)}><span>{cue ? 3 : m.evidence.length ? 2 : 1}</span><strong>Compare with a reference window · optional</strong><ArrowUpRight size={12}/></button></li>\n               <li><button onClick={() => exportReport(m)}><span>{cue ? 4 : m.evidence.length ? 3 : 2}</span><strong>Export incident handoff (.md)</strong><Download size={13}/></button></li>\n","move_path":null},"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/investigationReport.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -135,3 +135,3 @@\n     '',\n-    '## Review before handoff',\n+    '## Cross-check before handoff',\n     '',\n","move_path":null},"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/docs/submission/DEMO.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -14,6 +14,6 @@\n |---|---|---|\n-| 0:00–0:15 | Start on the selected publisher event and click **Analyze interval** | “The robot stopped at 6.187 seconds. A controls engineer receives a timestamp and seven synchronized traces, then has to prepare a handoff for the controls lead or vendor.” |\n+| 0:00–0:15 | Start on the selected publisher event and click **Analyze interval** | “An incident was annotated at 6.187 seconds. A controls engineer receives that timestamp and seven synchronized traces, then has to prepare a handoff for the controls lead or vendor.” |\n | 0:15–0:35 | Replay the 1.024-second interval at 0.5× while inference runs | “Trace keeps the publisher annotation, exact 7×1,024 model input and replay context together. The marker starts the investigation; it is not a verified cause or model detection.” |\n | 0:35–0:55 | Read the prediction and click **Show predicted moment in 3D** | “OpenTSLM predicts accidental contact, J4 and a relative onset. The robot jumps to that generated time cue. This is recorded articulation, not a reconstructed collision.” |\n-| 0:55–1:15 | Point to **Review note**, then click **Inspect exact seven-channel input** | “The model highlights J4, while J2 has the largest measured torque range. Trace exposes that disagreement and links back to the exact signals instead of hiding it in prose.” |\n+| 0:55–1:15 | Point to **Cross-check**, then click **Inspect exact seven-channel input** | “The model predicts J4 as strongest, while J2 has the largest raw torque range. Those are different rankings. Trace links both back to the exact signals instead of hiding the distinction in prose.” |\n | 1:15–1:30 | Click **Compare with a reference window** | “Against an earlier raw window, J2's measured range increases by 2.963 newton-metres. We ask the engineer to confirm motion phase and payload before attributing a cause.” |\n","move_path":null},"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/predictionReview.test.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -14,6 +14,6 @@\n describe('prediction review', () => {\n-  it('flags a visible model and measurement disagreement', () => {\n+  it('surfaces a cross-check between model and measurement rankings', () => {\n     expect(reviewPrediction(data, { start: 0, end: .002 }, prediction('J4'))).toEqual({\n       predictedJoint: 'J4', largestRangeJoint: 'J2',\n-      note: 'OpenTSLM highlights J4, while J2 has the largest measured torque range. Review both signals before sharing this handoff.',\n+      note: 'OpenTSLM predicts J4 as the strongest disturbance. J2 has the largest measured torque range. These are different quantities; inspect both before handoff.',\n     });\n","move_path":null},"/Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/investigationReport.test.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -77,3 +77,3 @@\n     expect(markdown).toContain('## Interpretation');\n-    expect(markdown).toContain('## Review before handoff');\n+    expect(markdown).toContain('## Cross-check before handoff');\n     expect(markdown).toContain('## Measured torque');\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/predictionReview.ts\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/predictionReview.test.ts\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/AssistantPanel.tsx\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/investigationReport.ts\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/frontend/src/assistant/investigationReport.test.ts\nM /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/docs/submission/DEMO.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789260178509,"completed_at_ms":1789260178836}}
