{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:45:15.739Z","ordinal":5369,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f21768c087d29901dec1752c84a9","summary_text":["**Evaluating UI issues**\n\nI'm noticing a potential problem with the custom question auto-expanding during analysis, especially when things are busy. This could be adding unnecessary clutter, which the user previously mentioned wanting to avoid. It seems like the code has the custom composer expand when busy, affecting the chat flow. I think we should keep the composer collapsed during analysis and add a visible Stop control instead. This might prevent the page from shifting and improve the overall experience."],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1789260311452,"completed_at_ms":1789260315739}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:45:15.742Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f21768c087d29901dec1752c84a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d"},"summary":[{"text":"**Evaluating UI issues**\n\nI'm noticing a potential problem with the custom question auto-expanding during analysis, especially when things are busy. This could be adding unnecessary clutter, which the user previously mentioned wanting to avoid. It seems like the code has the custom composer expand when busy, affecting the chat flow. I think we should keep the composer collapsed during analysis and add a visible Stop control instead. This might prevent the page from shifting and improve the overall experience.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:45:16.551Z","ordinal":5371,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f21bb36087d2abbf90b4eb2c87d1","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The live run exposed a real remaining UX bug: starting analysis expands the custom-question composer, which shifts the panel and recreates the “jumping” behavior. I’m fixing that now by keeping the form collapsed and turning the primary action into a stable Stop control while inference runs."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789260315744,"completed_at_ms":1789260316551}}
