{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:47:16.584Z","ordinal":5494,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f6a0c07b-5c67-494e-a291-a25a72bad64e","process_id":"41400","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority|OpenTSLM was fine-tuned|Legacy positive-contact\" model_training docs --glob '*.py' --glob '*.md' | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority|OpenTSLM was fine-tuned|Legacy positive-contact' model_training docs --glob '*.py' --glob '*.md'","query":"These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority|OpenTSLM was fine-tuned|Legacy positive-contact","path":"model_training"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:21:The signal-feature baseline outperforms this OpenTSLM checkpoint on semantics, joint ranking, and successful localization within 50 ms. OpenTSLM has higher onset coverage and slightly lower conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:25:OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training and representation together. Qwen frequently emitted null contact fields: JSON parsing and matching keys did not mean usable answers. No plain-Llama baseline was run in these artifacts.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:27:Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds contact macro-F1, answer coverage, strict usable-summary rate, and abstention columns in the JSON confusion matrices. It does not repair generations or substitute labels.\ndocs/submission/README.md:29:The contribution is a reproducible temporal-language investigation workflow and an honest account of where it works. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority. Deterministic measurements remain the source of numeric facts; generated semantics remain predictions. The stronger learned signal baseline currently belongs to offline evaluation and is not silently substituted for OpenTSLM in the app.\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:333:            \"conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:337:            \"OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training \"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:343:            \"Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds \"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:21:The signal-feature baseline outperforms this OpenTSLM checkpoint on semantics, joint ranking, and successful localization within 50 ms. OpenTSLM has higher onset coverage and slightly lower conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:25:OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training and representation together. Qwen frequently emitted null contact fields: JSON parsing and matching keys did not mean usable answers. No plain-Llama baseline was run in these artifacts.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:27:Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds contact macro-F1, answer coverage, strict usable-summary rate, and abstention columns in the JSON confusion matrices. It does not repair generations or substitute labels.\ndocs/submission/README.md:29:The contribution is a reproducible temporal-language investigation workflow and an honest account of where it works. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority. Deterministic measurements remain the source of numeric facts; generated semantics remain predictions. The stronger learned signal baseline currently belongs to offline evaluation and is not silently substituted for OpenTSLM in the app.\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:333:            \"conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:337:            \"OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training \"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:343:            \"Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds \"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2542},"formatted_output":"docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:21:The signal-feature baseline outperforms this OpenTSLM checkpoint on semantics, joint ranking, and successful localization within 50 ms. OpenTSLM has higher onset coverage and slightly lower conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:25:OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training and representation together. Qwen frequently emitted null contact fields: JSON parsing and matching keys did not mean usable answers. No plain-Llama baseline was run in these artifacts.\ndocs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md:27:Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds contact macro-F1, answer coverage, strict usable-summary rate, and abstention columns in the JSON confusion matrices. It does not repair generations or substitute labels.\ndocs/submission/README.md:29:The contribution is a reproducible temporal-language investigation workflow and an honest account of where it works. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority. Deterministic measurements remain the source of numeric facts; generated semantics remain predictions. The stronger learned signal baseline currently belongs to offline evaluation and is not silently substituted for OpenTSLM in the app.\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:333:            \"conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:337:            \"OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training \"\nmodel_training/src/robot_observability/comparison.py:343:            \"Legacy positive-contact F1 can stay high while free-motion answers are missing. This report adds \"\n"},"started_at_ms":1789260436584,"completed_at_ms":1789260436584}}
