{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:47:41.222Z","ordinal":5522,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ebe98b33-f24d-4bc1-b334-075366149ae9","process_id":"67214","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","PYTHONPATH=model_training/src python3 -m robot_observability.comparison --source docs/submission/evaluation/source --output /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2 && cmp /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.json docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.json && diff -u /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.md docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"PYTHONPATH=model_training/src python3 -m robot_observability.comparison --source docs/submission/evaluation/source --output /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2 && cmp /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.json docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.json && diff -u /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.md docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","stdout":"{\"windows\": 512, \"recordings\": 67, \"output\": \"/tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2\"}\n--- /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.md\t2026-09-13 02:47:41\n+++ docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md\t2026-09-13 02:17:11\n@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@\n | Affected-joint set F1 | 0.8228 | 0.8156 | 0.4396 | 271 contacts only; invalid lists score zero |\n | Onset MAE (ms) | 70.73 | 68.51 | 118.34 | Only finite in-window predictions; read with coverage |\n | Onset median error (ms) | 21.00 | 54.00 | 42.00 | Same conditional denominator as MAE |\n-| Onset P90 error (ms) | 188.60 | 140.00 | 313.80 | Same conditional denominator as MAE |\n | Onset coverage | 0.9410 | 0.9889 | 0.7860 | 271 contact windows |\n | Onset within 50 ms / all contacts | 0.5535 | 0.4649 | 0.4133 | 271; missing/invalid onsets fail |\n \n@@ -21,7 +20,7 @@\n \n The signal-feature baseline outperforms this OpenTSLM checkpoint on semantics, joint ranking, and successful localization within 50 ms. OpenTSLM has higher onset coverage and slightly lower conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\n \n-OpenTSLM returned no usable structured answer for 113 of 512 windows. That includes 112 of 241 free-motion windows (46.5%). On the 399 answered windows, semantics accuracy is 98.50% (393/399). This conditional figure is descriptive, not a paired comparison: the model selects which windows receive an answer, while the baseline answers every window. Any reliability fix must be selected on validation.\n+Decomposing the OpenTSLM confusion matrices: 113 of 512 windows received no usable structured answer, concentrated on free motion (112 of 241 free windows, 46.5%; 1 of 271 contact windows). On the 399 answered windows, semantics accuracy is 98.50% (393/399). The checkpoint's measured weakness is emitting a valid \"no event\" summary, not misclassifying answered windows. This conditional figure is descriptive, not a paired comparison: answered windows are model-selected, and the baseline answers all 512. The strongest-joint (0.7528 vs 0.8413) and within-50 ms localization gaps remain on answered windows.\n \n OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training and representation together. Qwen frequently emitted null contact fields: JSON parsing and matching keys did not mean usable answers. No plain-Llama baseline was run in these artifacts.\n \n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"windows\": 512, \"recordings\": 67, \"output\": \"/tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2\"}\n--- /tmp/trace-comparison-hardening-v2/comparison.md\t2026-09-13 02:47:41\n+++ docs/submission/evaluation/report/comparison.md\t2026-09-13 02:17:11\n@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@\n | Affected-joint set F1 | 0.8228 | 0.8156 | 0.4396 | 271 contacts only; invalid lists score zero |\n | Onset MAE (ms) | 70.73 | 68.51 | 118.34 | Only finite in-window predictions; read with coverage |\n | Onset median error (ms) | 21.00 | 54.00 | 42.00 | Same conditional denominator as MAE |\n-| Onset P90 error (ms) | 188.60 | 140.00 | 313.80 | Same conditional denominator as MAE |\n | Onset coverage | 0.9410 | 0.9889 | 0.7860 | 271 contact windows |\n | Onset within 50 ms / all contacts | 0.5535 | 0.4649 | 0.4133 | 271; missing/invalid onsets fail |\n \n@@ -21,7 +20,7 @@\n \n The signal-feature baseline outperforms this OpenTSLM checkpoint on semantics, joint ranking, and successful localization within 50 ms. OpenTSLM has higher onset coverage and slightly lower conditional mean onset error, but a worse median. These results do not establish OpenTSLM superiority.\n \n-OpenTSLM returned no usable structured answer for 113 of 512 windows. That includes 112 of 241 free-motion windows (46.5%). On the 399 answered windows, semantics accuracy is 98.50% (393/399). This conditional figure is descriptive, not a paired comparison: the model selects which windows receive an answer, while the baseline answers every window. Any reliability fix must be selected on validation.\n+Decomposing the OpenTSLM confusion matrices: 113 of 512 windows received no usable structured answer, concentrated on free motion (112 of 241 free windows, 46.5%; 1 of 271 contact windows). On the 399 answered windows, semantics accuracy is 98.50% (393/399). The checkpoint's measured weakness is emitting a valid \"no event\" summary, not misclassifying answered windows. This conditional figure is descriptive, not a paired comparison: answered windows are model-selected, and the baseline answers all 512. The strongest-joint (0.7528 vs 0.8413) and within-50 ms localization gaps remain on answered windows.\n \n OpenTSLM was fine-tuned; Qwen3-VL 4B was zero-shot on plots. This comparison changes training and repres