{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T00:48:12.162Z","ordinal":5549,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa5f2c4f8c087d2a0b9d62b5317c115","status":"completed","call_id":"call_wqk8KpGxsJf9xqJWdLx7oZIR","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/docs/submission/DEMO.md\\n@@\\n-Have the audited comparison and the exported JSON report open beside the app. If the live service is unavailable, explicitly present the committed smoke result as a previously recorded run; never present it as fresh inference.\\n+Have the audited comparison and a pre-run Markdown handoff open beside the app. If the live service is unavailable, explicitly present the committed smoke result as a previously recorded run; never present it as fresh inference.\\n@@\\n-| 0:35–0:55 | Read the prediction and click **Show predicted moment in 3D** | “OpenTSLM predicts accidental contact, J4 and a relative onset. The robot jumps to that generated time cue. This is recorded articulation, not a reconstructed collision.” |\\n+| 0:35–0:55 | Read the prediction and click **Show generated onset cue in 3D** | “OpenTSLM predicts accidental contact, J4 and a relative onset. The robot jumps to that generated time cue. This is recorded articulation, not a reconstructed collision.” |\\n@@\\n-| 1:15–1:30 | Click **Compare with a reference window** | “Against an earlier raw window, J2's measured range increases by 2.963 newton-metres. We ask the engineer to confirm motion phase and payload before attributing a cause.” |\\n-| 1:30–1:42 | Click **Export incident handoff** | “The Markdown report carries the recording, interval, annotation, measurements, model revision, input receipt, review note and limitations to the next engineer.” |\\n-| 1:42–1:55 | Open **Evaluation** | “On 512 windows from 67 held-out recording groups, simple features win fixed classification. OpenTSLM adds the readable evidence-linked investigation object, but only 77.93 percent of generations are usable. We show that weakness.” |\\n-| 1:55–2:00 | Return to the incident | “Trace turns one recorded stop into a reviewable handoff. The business hypothesis is less report assembly and back-and-forth; the prepared pilot still has to measure it.” |\\n+| 1:15–1:30 | Click **Compare with a reference window · optional** | “Against an earlier raw window, J2's measured range increases by 2.963 newton-metres. We ask the engineer to confirm motion phase and payload before attributing a cause.” |\\n+| 1:30–1:42 | Click **Export incident handoff (.md)** | “The Markdown report carries the recording, interval, annotation, measurements, model revision, input receipt, cross-check and limitations to the next engineer.” |\\n+| 1:42–1:55 | Open **Evaluation** | “On 512 windows from 67 held-out recording groups, simple features win fixed classification. Trace turns OpenTSLM's structured output into the readable, evidence-linked handoff, but only 77.93 percent of generations are usable. We show that weakness.” |\\n+| 1:55–2:00 | Return to the incident | “Trace turns one recorded incident into a reviewable handoff. The business hypothesis is less report assembly and back-and-forth; the prepared pilot still has to measure it.” |\\n*** Update File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/docs/submission/VERIFICATION.md\\n@@\\n-| Frontend, `npm test` | 81 passed, including structured prediction isolation, model/measurement disagreement, investigation provenance and replay contracts |\\n+| Frontend, `npm test` | 81 passed, including structured prediction isolation, model/measurement cross-checks, investigation provenance and replay contracts |\\n@@\\n-| Browser, desktop | Structured prediction, J4/J2 review note, predicted 3D moment, seven-channel evidence, reference comparison and Markdown export verified through the live UI |\\n+| Browser, desktop | Structured prediction, J4/J2 cross-check, generated 3D onset cue, seven-channel evidence, reference comparison, Markdown export and stable cancellation verified through the live UI |\\n*** Update File: /Users/sametdegirmenci/Downloads/ysamet/inference/README.md\\n@@\\n-  rejects other ranges and any window that is not exactly 1.024 seconds. It does not feed the reduced\\n-  100 Hz overview to the model. Full recording inference needs the ingestion/data\\n+  rejects other ranges and any window that is not exactly 1.024 seconds. It does\\n+  not feed the reduced 100 Hz overview to the model. Full recording inference needs the ingestion/data\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0982b-48a6-7a00-b4fb-0f363c602d5d","create_time":1789260479.582227}}}
